      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# ReCAP study — false-alarm calibration (causal eval)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Upload this notebook fresh** from `D:\\\\quant\\\\ReCAP\\\\notebooks\\\\study_run_colab.ipynb` after each push.\n",
        "\n",
        "This run produces the first **study** artifact (not just smoke):\n",
        "- fit once at default \(h=2.5\\sigma\)\n",
        "- calibrate thresholds on train for 0.5 / 1 / 2 alarms/year\n",
        "- causal test eval for default + calibrated variants\n",
        "- synthetic-shift detector diagnostic\n",
        "\n",
        "Uses **micro** profile for Colab RAM. Results are pilot-scale but protocol-correct."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "REPO_URL = \"https://github.com/laraib-b/ReCAP-study.git\"\n",
        "REPO_DIR = \"/content/ReCAP\"\n",
        "BRANCH = \"main\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import os, subprocess, sys\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "repo = Path(REPO_DIR)\n",
        "if not repo.exists():\n",
        "    subprocess.check_call([\"git\", \"clone\", \"--depth\", \"1\", \"-b\", BRANCH, REPO_URL, REPO_DIR])\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    subprocess.check_call([\"git\", \"-C\", REPO_DIR, \"fetch\", \"origin\", BRANCH])\n",
        "    subprocess.check_call([\"git\", \"-C\", REPO_DIR, \"reset\", \"--hard\", f\"origin/{BRANCH}\"])\n",
        "os.chdir(REPO_DIR)\n",
        "sys.path.insert(0, REPO_DIR)\n",
        "print(\"commit:\", subprocess.check_output([\"git\", \"rev-parse\", \"--short\", \"HEAD\"], text=True).strip())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "%pip install -q \"numpy>=1.24,<2.5\" \"pandas==2.2.3\" \"torch\" \"gymnasium>=0.29\" \"stable-baselines3>=2.0\" \"yfinance>=0.2\" \"requests>=2.31\"\n",
        "import os\n",
        "os.environ[\"YF_DISABLE_CURL_CFFI\"] = \"1\"\n",
        "print(\"deps ready\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Run study (micro)\n",
        "\n",
        "Expect several minutes to tens of minutes on CPU. Download `outputs/study/*.json` when done."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import torch\n",
        "device = \"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\"\n",
        "print(\"device:\", device)\n",
        "!python study/run_study.py --profile micro --dataset DOW30 --device {device} --seed 0 --disable-local-cache --no-adapt-control"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "import json\n",
        "files = sorted(Path(\"outputs/study\").glob(\"study_*.json\"))\n",
        "print(\"files:\", [p.name for p in files])\n",
        "if not files:\n",
        "    raise SystemExit(\"No study JSON found\")\n",
        "latest = files[-1]\n",
        "!python study/aggregate.py {latest}\n",
        "payload = json.loads(latest.read_text())\n",
        "print(\"variants:\", list(payload[\"results\"]))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## After success\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Download the latest `outputs/study/study_*.json` (+ `.md` if created).\n",
        "2. Message Cursor that the study run finished.\n",
        "3. Optional later: re-run with `--seed 1` then `--seed 2` for a 3-seed pilot."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
